            <ArticleTitle>Polycatenation tuned microporosity of two metal-tris(4'-carboxybiphenyl)amine frameworks with multilayer structures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13352-13355</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7dt02976d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>By employing a nanosized tris(4'-carboxybiphenyl)amine ligand to assemble with Zn2+ ions, a novel trilayer network (FIR-37) and an unprecedented 2D → 3D microporous polycatenation framework (FIR-38) based on unusual tetralayers have been synthesized and structurally characterized. FIR-38 shows permanent porosity with a Langmuir surface area of 1408.4 m2 g-1.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
